ukberi-tibyan:129-129.t:
Allah the Exalted said: {رَبنَا وَابعث فيهم رَسُولا مِنْهُم يَتْلُو عَلَيْهِم آياتك}
His saying, Exalted is He: (وَابْعَثْ فِيهِمْ): [the pronoun] is in the masculine plural according to the meaning of الْأُمَّة; had He said فِيهَا, it would have referred to the wording of الْأُمَّة. يَتْلُو عَلَيْهِمْ is in the position of the accusative as an adjective (ṣifa) of رَسُولًا.
It may also be a ḥāl (circumstantial) from the pronoun in مِنْهُمْ, and what governs it is the [implied notion of] settledness (al-istiqrār).
